    duplicate_of: []  # ce09
    not_duplicate_of: []  # ce09
    pr_ref:  # ce09
    description: "Found by the 2026-09-17 fundamental concept audit of the pass-silence host\nboundary. Write-up: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-pass-silence-host-boundary_09172026.md\n\nTWO FINDINGS, ONE SITE. A behavioral bug, and the refutation of the stated\nground for the two-host split.\n\n=== 1. THE BUG (live repro) ===\n\nanalyze/base.py:4005-4022, the grammar-unavailable path:\n\n    run.warnings.append(f\"UserWarning: {msg}\")     # <- INV-pitab\n    warnings.warn(msg, UserWarning, stacklevel=2)\n    run.duration_ms = int((time.time() - start_time) * 1000)\n    return AnalysisResult(run=run, skipped=True, ...,\n                          skip_reason_code=DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE)\n\nThe comment above that append says, verbatim: \"INV-pitab: structurally record\nthe warning on the run so consumers reading the AnalysisRun later see the gap.\"\n\ncollect_analyzer_result then does analysis_runs.append(result.run.to_dict())\nONLY in the else of `if is_skipped:`. The run is built, stamped, and dropped.\n\nREPRO (ran 2026-09-17 at d0a2171dc5):\n\n    run = AnalysisRun(execution_id=\"x1\", pass_id=\"java\", version=\"8.0.0\")\n    run.warnings.append(\"UserWarning: java analysis skipped: grammar not available...\")\n    run.duration_ms = 42\n    res = AnalysisResult(run=run, skipped=True,\n                         skip_reason=\"java tree-sitter grammar not available\",\n                         skip_reason_code=\"dependency_unavailable\")\n    collect_analyzer_result(res, runs, [], [], [], Limits(), analyzer_name=\"java\")\n\n    analysis_runs serialized : []\n    skipped_passes           : [{'pass': 'java', 'reason': '...', 'skip_reason_code': 'dependency_unavailable'}]\n    WARNING SURVIVED TO OUTPUT: False\n    duration_ms SURVIVED     : False\n\nSo INV-pitab's structural record is dead for exactly the population it was\nwritten for. The warnings.warn call still reaches stderr, so a user in a bare\nenvironment is not blind -- but a CONSUMER of the behavior map is, which is\nwhat INV-pitab was about. Same shape at 39 other dependency_unavailable sites\nand all 7 pass_crashed analyzer sites.\n\n=== 2. THE STATED GROUND FOR THE SPLIT IS FALSE ===\n\npass_silence.py, the \"skipped_passes half of the axis\" comment block:\n\n  \"a pass that is `dependency_unavailable`, `backend_disabled` or\n   `pass_crashed` HAS NO AnalysisRun ... There is no carrier in existence to\n   stamp.\"\n\nFor dependency_unavailable that is not true: base.py:4017 returns `run=run`.\nThe carrier exists, carries a warning and a duration, and is discarded by\npolicy. Repeated in schema.py:101 and docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:1317.\n\nThe POLICY may still be right. Only its stated ground is wrong, and it is\nwrong in the direction that makes the policy look forced rather than chosen.\n\n=== 3. WHY THIS CHANGES A DECISION ALREADY RESERVED TO THE OWNER ===\n\nADR-0056 §\"What would change this decision\" item 5 reserves to the owner:\n\"An owner ruling that AnalysisRun should be emitted for passes that did not\nrun. That dissolves the re-hosting finding entirely and collapses 3+1 to a\nflat 4. This ADR judges it wrong -- an AnalysisRun for a pass that never ran\nis ABSENT != EMPTY one level up -- but it is the owner's call, and it is the\nsingle assumption the class analysis rests on.\"\n\nThe audit sharpens the question the owner was asked. It is NOT \"should we\nCREATE an AnalysisRun for a pass that never ran\". For the 40 grammar-gated\nanalyzers it is \"should we KEEP the one we already made\". Those passes DID\nstart: they were dispatched, they timed themselves, they built a run and\nappended a warning to it, and only then discovered the grammar was missing.\nThe ADR's objection (ABSENT != EMPTY) is materially weaker against a pass that\nbegan work than against one that never ran, and the ADR did not know the run\nexisted when it made the judgement.\n\nSIBLING ROW: WI-luvud is the mirror image -- rust-analyzer's backend returns\nNone and the pass files a SKIP although it RAN. Same boundary, opposite side.\nBoth should be decided together, and neither should be decided by an agent.\n\nSIZING: the bug alone is one chokepoint and a test. The accounting question is\nthe work, and it is the owner's."  # ce09
    fields: {}  # ce09
- op: discuss  # 5110
  at: '2026-09-17T19:29:21Z'  # 5110
