  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5110
  clock: 2  # 5110
  nonce: '5110'  # 5110
  message: "CORRECTION TO THIS ROW, from the owner's question \"does the discarded record\nhave anything of value?\". It largely does not, and two claims in the original\ndescription are wrong. Re-pointing rather than striking.\n\nWHAT IS ACTUALLY ON THE DISCARDED RECORD. Forced a missing grammar on\nCSharpAnalyzer and dumped run.to_dict():\n\n    execution_id       uuid:1c86b3c9-...      referenced by nothing (0 symbols, 0 edges)\n    run_signature      sha256:467595d0...\n    pass               csharp                 already in the skip entry\n    version            8.0.0                  global, on every record\n    toolchain          {name: python, version: 3.12.3}   <- THE DEFAULT\n    config_fingerprint sha256:44136fa355b3678a            <- sha256 of {}, the\n                                                             literal default\n                                                             INV-lidul exists to\n                                                             eliminate\n    files_analyzed 0   files_skipped 0   duration_ms 0\n    nodes_emitted 0    edges_emitted 0   pass_version \"\"\n    warnings           ABSENT\n\nThe punchline is the toolchain field. _extend_toolchain exists specifically to\nrecord tree_sitter_version / grammar_module / grammar_version -- the strongest\ncandidate reason to keep the record -- and it adds NOTHING here, because the\ngrammar whose version it would report is the thing that is missing. The field\nthat would justify keeping the record is empty exactly in the case where the\nrecord is discarded.\n\nEverything non-default on it is already in the skipped_passes entry.\n\nCORRECTION 1. The original description says the discard has \"the same shape at\n39 other dependency_unavailable sites and all 7 pass_crashed analyzer sites\",\nimplying they all lose a warning. Measured: of 42 DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE sites,\nexactly ONE (base.py:4021) appends the warning to the run. The other 41 call\nwarnings.warn() only -- stderr, never touching the record. csharp builds a run,\nwarns, and returns with run.warnings == []. The warning loss is ONE SITE WIDE,\nnot forty.\n\nCORRECTION 2. The discard itself is still real and still applies to every\nskipped result, but \"the record is discarded\" is only a defect if the record\ncarries something. It does not.\n\nWHAT IS ACTUALLY LOST, AND IT IS SMALL AND CHEAP. The install advice. base.py's\nwarning text is \"{lang} analysis skipped: grammar not available. Install the\nrequired tree-sitter grammar package.\" -- the actionable half. The retained\nskip_reason is \"{lang} tree-sitter grammar not available\" -- the\nnon-actionable half.\n\nAnd that generalises. Of 45 AnalysisResult(skip_reason=...) sites in the tree,\nexactly ONE carries install advice (r_lang.py:433, \"pip install\ntree-sitter-language-pack\"). The other 44 stop at \"grammar not available\".\nMeanwhile pass_silence.py justifies keeping the prose reason alongside the code\non the grounds that it \"carries the pip command and the exception message,\npayload a code cannot express\". For 44 of 45 sites it carries no such thing.\n\nRECOMMENDED RE-POINT (owner's call, hence no status/priority change made here):\n  - DOWNGRADE. The AnalysisRun-vs-skip accounting question this row raised is\n    close to moot on the evidence: there is nothing on the record to keep, so\n    the ADR-0056 item 5 re-framing in the original description carries much\n    less weight than written. It does not disappear -- a pass that began work\n    is still not a pass that never ran -- but it should not be decided on the\n    strength of \"we are throwing away a populated record\", because we are not.\n  - The cheap real fix is unrelated to the host question: put the install\n    advice into skip_reason at the 44 sites that lack it, where pass_silence.py\n    already claims it lives. No schema change, no owner decision.\n  - The genuine owner questions are elsewhere and do not depend on this:\n    WI-luvud (a pass that really ran, filed as not having run) and WI-mamiv\n    (the host boundary itself).\n\nThe lab-notebook write-up has been corrected in the same pass."  # 5110
